00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:18.240
as Peter Osborne and Andrew Saul,
recommending mega doses of antioxidants

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:24.510
like vitamin A, C, and D, as a means to
protect against COVID19. Not only are

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:29.360
these recommendations not supported by
the evidence, but they may actually be

00:18:29.360 --> 00:18:34.740
extremely dangerous. These people are
recommending doses that are way beyond

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:39.450
the recommended amounts for each vitamin and they pose some serious health risks.

00:18:39.450 --> 00:18:43.710
Vitamin C, for example, does have a role
in immunity and wound healing and can be

00:18:43.710 --> 00:18:47.760
obtained from the diet by eating a
variety of fruits and vegetables. Because

00:18:47.760 --> 00:18:53.370
vitamin C is water-soluble, it does not
get stored in the body and any excess is

00:18:53.370 --> 00:18:58.230
excreted out in your pee. However, this
is mostly true for food sources of

00:18:58.230 --> 00:19:03.690
vitamin C. Whereas, supplemental forms of
vitamin C are not excreted as easily

00:19:03.690 --> 00:19:09.510
from the body leading to an increased
risk of toxicity. One 2019 review did find

00:19:09.510 --> 00:19:15.450
that oral and IV high doses of vitamin C
treatment may reduce ICU stay by 8% and

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:21.480
shortened ventillation duration by 18.2%.
However, in practice, including early

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:25.740
experiments with COVID 19 patients,
doctors would never give these high

00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:29.850
amounts orally. They would need to be
administered through an IV very

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:34.650
carefully monitored by a doctor.
The reason is that excess vitamin C

00:19:34.650 --> 00:19:38.940
supplementation is not necessarily
benign. Excess vitamin C supplementation

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:43.440
can cause adverse health effects ranging
from digestive symptoms, like diarrhea

00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:48.570
and nausea, to the development of kidney
stones and it may also lead to iron

00:19:48.570 --> 00:19:54.179
overload which can be seriously damaging
for organs like the heart, liver, and

00:19:54.179 --> 00:19:57.000
pancreas.
These adverse effects appear to occur

00:19:57.000 --> 00:20:02.130
when people are taking vitamin C doses
just over 2,000 milligrams. And our

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:08.570
friends, Peter Osborne and Andrew Saul,
are recommending between 5,000 and

00:20:08.570 --> 00:20:13.200
24,000 milligrams.
Folks, you may not need to go to the ER

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:18.300
for COVID but you'll be praying they
have a bed when your liver fails. As for

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:22.650
vitamin D, low levels of vitamin D have
been associated with respiratory disease

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:27.390
as well as viral respiratory infections
and decreased lung function. While we

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:32.070
don't have actual research on vitamin D
for COVID,  it does make sense that we

00:20:32.070 --> 00:20:36.390
would want to keep our vitamin levels in
check especially considering the high

00:20:36.390 --> 00:20:41.280
prevalence of vitamin D deficiency
worldwide. But as for high single doses, a

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:46.320
systematic review concluded that single
doses of vitamin D up to a hundred

00:20:46.320 --> 00:20:50.880
thousand IUs may be effective at
improving vitamin D status to prevent

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:53.730
deficiency while under medical
supervision.

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:58.110
Mind you, these are findings not
recommendations and they pertain to a

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:03.870
single dose every three months not daily
dosages. Also, similar to vitamin C,

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:08.610
vitamin D also has potential risks from
high supplemental doses, including

00:21:08.610 --> 00:21:12.930
elevated calcium levels, digestive
symptoms, dizziness, confusion, nausea,

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:18.840
vomiting, stomach pain, bone loss, and even kidney failure. Toxicity is also more

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:23.400
likely to occur in people taking high
dose supplements, as it is very unlikely

00:21:23.400 --> 00:21:28.590
to reach high blood levels through diet
alone. Contrary to vitamin C, vitamin D is

00:21:28.590 --> 00:21:33.000
fat soluble meaning it's stored in the
body fat and released into the

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:38.040
bloodstream slowly versus being excreted
immediately in the urine. Because we're

00:21:38.040 --> 00:21:42.570
able to have vitamin D stores, this means
that the effects of vitamin D toxicity

00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:47.940
may potentially last for several months
after you stop taking the supplements.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:53.220
So the recommended daily amounts for adults is just 600 IUs compared to Peter

00:21:53.220 --> 00:21:58.380
Osborne's recommendation of a 150,000 IUs of vitamin D.

00:21:58.380 --> 00:22:02.040
I am pretty good at taking a lot of
supplements at once, but I would have to

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:08.370
take 250 vitamin D tablets per day just
to reach those recommendations.

00:22:08.370 --> 00:22:13.410
That would work out to around $300 per week. Nope!

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:18.420
As for the risks of high supplemental
doses of vitamin A, they may include

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:24.450
vision changes, bone pain, skin changes,
respiratory infection, and possible

00:22:24.450 --> 00:22:29.550
kidney and liver damage. Peter Osborne
recommends 7500 micrograms of vitamin A

00:22:29.550 --> 00:22:35.070
which is more than eight times the
recommended daily amount of 700 to 900

00:22:35.070 --> 00:22:41.100
micrograms for adults. So yeah, just
please don't. Bottom line, there is

00:22:41.100 --> 00:22:45.150
absolutely nothing safe about taking
mega doses of vitamin supplements

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:51.000
without medical supervision as these can
cause some serious adverse health risks

00:22:51.000 --> 00:22:56.130
which may even land you in the hospital.
And that is probably the last place you

00:22:56.130 --> 00:23:03.000
want to be during a global pandemic. So,
please save your money, get your vitamins

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:08.340
mainly from food sources, take your usual
vitamin doses, and talk to a doctor or

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:12.600
dietitian before starting any new
supplements. Now I want to just conclude

00:23:12.600 --> 00:23:19.800
with some general immunity tips. So the
big question, coronavirus or no

00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:24.120
coronavirus, is there anything that we
can do naturally to support our immune

00:23:24.120 --> 00:23:28.890
system for general health and well-being
according to the research? The answer is

00:23:28.890 --> 00:23:33.660
yes there is. Though no one food or
supplement can prevent illness or

00:23:33.660 --> 00:23:37.590
infection, you can always support your
immune system through a balanced diet

00:23:37.590 --> 00:23:43.460
that includes adequate sources of
protein like lean meat, poultry, fish, eggs,

00:23:43.460 --> 00:23:49.380
tofu, beans, legumes. Vitamin A from
sources like orange or yellow vegetables

00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:54.000
and fruits, and dark leafy greens. Vitamin
C from things like citrus fruits and a

00:23:54.000 --> 00:23:58.350
wide variety of vegetables. Vitamin E
from healthy fat sources like nuts and

00:23:58.350 --> 00:24:04.110
oils. And zinc from whole grains, beans,
nuts, and animal protein. In addition to

00:24:04.110 --> 00:24:07.740
supporting the immune system through
food, you can also support a healthy

00:24:07.740 --> 00:24:12.240
immune system through lifestyle changes
by getting adequate sleep, exercising

00:24:12.240 --> 00:24:18.030
regularly, and managing stress. Bottom
line, though "immunity boosting" sure is a

00:24:18.030 --> 00:24:21.090
buzzword these days,
the reality is there

00:24:21.090 --> 00:24:26.550
is currently no known cures or
preventative treatments for COVID 19.

00:24:26.550 --> 00:24:31.680
Though research is still underway to
develop a vaccine, no food or product on

00:24:31.680 --> 00:24:36.180
the market can promise immunity or
protection from this virus. So be

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:39.180
skeptical of anyone trying to sell or
promote a product that makes these

00:24:39.180 --> 00:24:43.950
extreme and sensationalized promises.
Also, be skeptical of anyone who

00:24:43.950 --> 00:24:47.910
simultaneously tries to sell these
themselves without giving alternative

00:24:47.910 --> 00:24:51.990
product suggestions. Again, I want to
emphasize that while taking care of your

00:24:51.990 --> 00:24:57.780
general health should always be a
priority, not just in a pandemic, the most

00:24:57.780 --> 00:25:00.990
important things that you can
immediately do to protect yourself and

00:25:00.990 --> 00:25:06.330
others is to wash your hands, avoid
touching your face, and practice social

00:25:06.330 --> 00:25:11.010
distancing. Well folks, that is all for
this episode of The Ridiculist. Please

00:25:11.010 --> 00:25:15.660
continue to stay safe and stay critical
